          "id": "markets-muhurat-trading-2026-11-08",
          "headline": "Sensex, Nifty slip in Muhurat trading, ending a long Diwali winning run",
          "summary": "In the one-hour Diwali session that opens Samvat 2083, the Sensex rose over 400 points early to about 81,406 but closed 29 points lower at 80,999.40; the Nifty fell 44 points, or 0.18%, to 24,986.40. Smaller stocks did better: the Nifty Smallcap 100 gained about 1%, and Sun Pharma and Tata Steel led the Sensex while M&M and IndiGo lagged.",
          "why_it_matters": "After the best week since 2021, the flat finish suggests traders are booking some profit before Monday's full session.",
